#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Rust compiler {#install-the-rust-compiler}"
msgstr "Installer le compilateur Rust {#install-the-rust-compiler}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A Rust compiler must be installed on your system to compile Qiskit. To "
"install the Rust compiler, use the cross-platform Rust installer "
"[`rustup`](https://rustup.rs/) or [another install "
"method](https://forge.rust-lang.org/infra/other-installation-"
"methods.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"Un compilateur Rust doit être installé sur ton système pour compiler Qiskit."
" Pour installer le compilateur Rust, utilise l'installateur Rust "
"multiplateforme [`rustup`](https://rustup.rs/) ou [une autre méthode "
"d'installation](https://forge.rust-lang.org/infra/other-installation-"
"methods.html).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install Qiskit {#install-qiskit}"
msgstr "Installer Qiskit {#install-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Follow these steps to install Qiskit:\n"
msgstr "Suis ces étapes pour installer Qiskit :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clone the Qiskit repository.\n"
msgstr "Clone le dépôt Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change to the `qiskit` directory.\n"
msgstr "Accède au répertoire `qiskit`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(Optional) If you want to run tests or linting checks, install the developer"
" requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"(Optionnel) Si tu veux exécuter des tests ou des vérifications de linting, "
"installe les dépendances de développement.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install `qiskit`.\n"
msgstr "Installe `qiskit`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Standard install**:\n"
msgstr "**Installation standard** :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install .\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install .\n"
"    ```\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Editable mode**: In this mode, you don't need to reinstall Qiskit when "
"there are code changes to the project.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mode éditable** : Dans ce mode, tu n'as pas besoin de réinstaller Qiskit "
"lorsqu'il y a des modifications de code dans le projet.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install -e .\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install -e .\n"
"    ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    In editable mode, the compiled extensions are built in _debug mode_ "
"without optimizations. This affects the runtime performance of the compiled "
"code. To build the compiled extensions with optimizations enabled, run the "
"following command to rebuild the binary in _release mode_:\n"
msgstr ""
"    En mode éditable, les extensions compilées sont construites en _mode "
"debug_ sans optimisations. Cela affecte les performances à l'exécution du "
"code compilé. Pour construire les extensions compilées avec les "
"optimisations activées, exécute la commande suivante pour reconstruire le "
"binaire en _mode release_ :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    python setup.py build_rust --release --inplace\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    python setup.py build_rust --release --inplace\n"
"    ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    If you are working on Rust code in Qiskit, you need to rebuild the extension code every time you make a local change. In editable mode, the Rust extension is only built when the install command is run, so local changes you make to the Rust code are not reflected in the installed package unless you rebuild the extension by rerunning `build_rust` (with or without `--release`, depending on whether you want to build in release or debug mode).\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    Si tu travailles sur du code Rust dans Qiskit, tu dois reconstruire le code de l'extension à chaque fois que tu effectues une modification locale. En mode éditable, l'extension Rust n'est construite que lors de l'exécution de la commande d'installation, donc les modifications locales apportées au code Rust ne sont pas reflétées dans le package installé, sauf si tu reconstruis l'extension en réexécutant `build_rust` (avec ou sans `--release`, selon que tu veux construire en mode release ou debug).\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Étapes suivantes {#next-steps}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"  - Read the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) to contribute to the open-source Qiskit SDK.\n"
"  - [Run your first quantum circuit](/guides/quick-start).\n"
"  - Try a tutorial, such as [Grover's algorithm](/tutorials/grovers-algorithm).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommandations\">\n"
"  - Lis les [directives de contribution](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) pour contribuer au SDK Qiskit open source.\n"
"  - [Exécute ton premier circuit quantique](/guides/quick-start).\n"
"  - Essaie un tutoriel, comme [l'algorithme de Grover](/tutorials/grovers-algorithm).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
